.TH RECOPY 1 "November 2025" "recopy project"
.SH NAME
recopy \- smart cp/mv replacement with reflink, rsync, and btrfs fast paths.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B recopy
.RI [ options ] " SRC... DEST"
.br
.B recopy doctor
.SH DESCRIPTION
recopy plans copy or move operations using rename/reflink fast paths locally and rsync or btrfs send/receive remotely. The CLI mirrors familiar cp semantics while exposing flags to control transport, parallelism, verification, and UI output.
.PP
The
.B doctor
subcommand inspects common runtime dependencies (rsync, ssh, optional btrfs + hyperfine) and reports readiness for typical workflows.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --move
Prefer rename when SRC and DEST share a filesystem; fallback to rsync.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Plan only and show the execution steps without mutating data.
.TP
.B --mirror
Delete extraneous files from DEST similar to rsync --delete-delay.
.TP
.B --profile auto|lan|wan
Apply compression + prescan presets.
.TP
.B --parallel N
Limit worker count for rsync transfers (default 1).
.TP
.B --transport auto|rsync|btrfs
Force a transport or let recopy choose.
.TP
.B --no-reflink
Disable reflink attempts even when supported.
.TP
.B --inplace
Use rsync --inplace instead of temp files.
.TP
.B --prescan, --verify, --one-file-system, --no-ui
Fine tune metadata scanning, verification, traversal, and TUI output.
.SH FILES
The repository ships sample shell completions under
.I completions/
for bash and zsh users, plus this man page at
.I docs/recopy.1
for local installs.
.SH SEE ALSO
cp(1), mv(1), rsync(1), btrfs(8)
